# Coding Etiquette

Full rules live in `AGENTS.md`. Read it before writing or editing code or docs. Highlights:

- Never download or install anything yourself; add it to `scripts/owner/install-deps.sh` and wait for the owner.
- Flashing goes through `./crush80`. New images boot as a trial and the host confirms them. A hash-verified known-good image must exist first.
- Docs: `docs/features/` (current design), `docs/guides/` (how-to), `docs/code/<mirror>.md` (per-file why), `docs/decisions/` (append-only), `docs/incidents/`.
- Comments explain why, never what. No AI-slop prose. Extract instead of growing a function that keeps collecting special cases.
- Every command in a script has a timeout. Every host-side feature has tests; safety invariants get named tests.
- Commit only when asked, staging explicit paths, after `bash scripts/gate/verify.sh` is green.

Do not duplicate `AGENTS.md` here; update that file instead.
